      "message": "feat(machines): the plain Tormach xsTECH Router\n\nInch machine file for the original xsTECH Router, from Tormach's public\npages (no manual exists): spec sheet 02/25, product and package pages,\nand the knowledge base. Travel 8.6 x 6.3 x 2.4 in; spindle 5000-15000\nrpm at 0.08 kW - the narrowest window and smallest motor the sources\nstate, as the spindle changed between builds; 120 IPM on every axis;\nmanual ER11 collet (no ATC stated); no rigid tapping, no coolant; safe\nretract Z0. Registered in posting::MACHINES as a mill, so it posts\nthrough the PathPilot post. tormach_routers pins its figures, the post\n(now at S12000, inside every router's window) and the spindle window\nrefusals.\n\nFixes #620\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
